/-!
# All-row-two pure-first native geometry

Exports the pair, whole-kernel, and whole-centralizer reductions, uniqueness
of a certified-eight container over a plane, and a concrete native obstruction
to unrestricted eight containment. Intrinsic point-core shears prove whole-
normalizer transitivity and exclude invariant planes; the canonical point-core
intersection preserves the maximal-two-local normalizer and radical restriction.
Distinct point-core intersections are elementary of order at most 128; the
marked intersection has an exhaustive list of exactly 128 native words. One
conjugator places the original group and its canonical sixteen-overgroup join
in this container. The join has the same maximal-two-local normalizer, with
literal radical restriction maps. The shared line row has its unconditional
whole max4 normalizer and literal radical restriction. All twenty-five nonline
rows have actual whole-subgroup F placements. A first-class point lies in
exactly 330 ambient F occurrences, and the seed F occurrence has a certified
128-word intersection with the native point core, transported through max2
words. The complete ambient occurrence incidence table certifies a second-class
member of every nonline row's canonical F intersection. This invariant
intersection controls the whole normalizer. The exhaustive finite census
identifies every original all-row-two subgroup with one of the rows, so the
maximal-two-local named-local endpoint of Kleidman--Wilson (1988), Section 2.1,
and its literal arbitrary-radical restriction are unconditional under the
original purity, order and no-native-pair hypotheses. The separate
native-pair-contained branch remains with the elementary-cover assembly.
-/
